# Hero mobile cover — subject must stay in frame (learned 2026-09-24)

Charcoal left copy and “show the child/family” fight on **one** 16:9 file when the box is portrait `object-cover`. Fix the **class** (shared cover focus + photo safe-zone), not only homepage `hero-3`.

## Two boxes (do not treat as one)

| Surface | Box | Crop today | Text |
|---|---|---|---|
| Homepage Swiper (`app/page.tsx`) | `min-h-screen` / `h-screen` | `object-cover` + charcoal → `object-left` below `lg` (1024) | Slide 3 charcoal; 1–2 white-center |
| Market S / Stickers / Stamp / Phone Cases | Short banner ~300–420px | `SlidingBackground` `bg-cover` **`bg-center` always** | **Charcoal left** (`CategoryCharcoalHero`) |

Live family file ~**1280×714** (1.79:1). Child sits **right**. Phone portrait home left-pin shows ~25–31% **left wall only**. Market S banner still center-crops ~15% each side, so a far-right child can vanish there too.

Do **not** lower homepage Swiper height to “fix” slide 3 — slides 1–2 share that height (hero video protected).

## Invariant

On phones, the **subject** (child / faces / product in the photo) must remain inside the visible crop. Charcoal is an HTML wash; it does **not** require the left wall to be the only thing on screen.

## What to change (when owner asks to apply)

1. **Shared cover focus** — one helper (e.g. `lib/heroCoverFocus.ts`): percentage `object-position` / `background-position` (default `70% 50%` for family/right-subject; `50% 50%` for centered product shots). Use on homepage `ImageSlide` **and** `SlidingBackground` `ImageSlide`. Do not hardcode `object-left` only because overlay is charcoal.
2. **Homepage charcoal** — stop `homeHeroCoverObjectPosition` → `'left'` for this class of photo. Wash still darkens the left for type. Optional CMS `coverFocus` later; until then right-subject slides use ~70% not 0%.
3. **Category heroes** — Stickers / Market S / Stamp / Phone Cases storefront overlay is charcoal (`CategoryCharcoalHero`). New admin rows default **Effect = fade**. `slide` pan/tile still hides subjects if someone picks it.
4. **Do not** add `srcMobile` unless homepage must stay full-viewport **and** one landscape file still fails after focus ~70%. Portrait second asset is the fallback, not the first patch.

## Owner photo spec (Stickers upload + Market S / home slide 3)

Landscape **1920×800** (~2.4:1) or **1920×1080**. Keep faces/child in the **safe zone**:

| Overlay | Horizontal (from left) | Vertical |
|---|---|---|
| Charcoal (Market S, Stickers hub, home slide 3, Stamp/Phone Cases when active) | **40–80%** (left 0–35% empty wall/negative space) | Middle ~60% |

Avoid 1:1. Avoid putting the only subject on the far right edge. Admin list preview is a small 16:9 tile — **not** a phone crop; check a 390px-wide viewport. Stickers hub is charcoal like Market S — uploading a photo does **not** by itself switch overlay; `CategoryCharcoalHero` is the storefront overlay.

## Cousins (same class)

- iPad portrait width **&lt; 1024** still uses homepage left-pin today
- Stickers / Stamp / Phone Cases share `SlidingBackground` — a Stickers-only `bg-right` fork would miss Market S and future Stamp re-enable
- Effect `zoom` scales 1.2 → extra crop; `rotate` unusable for people
- Homepage slide 1 video is `object-contain` (different); slide 2 1:1 is worse cover
- `/stickers/[slug]` listing has **no** category hero — hub `/stickers` only
- `responsive.mobile` on category slides is speed/opacity only, **not** a second image

## Do not

- Pin `object-left` to “save charcoal” when the subject is on the right
- Redesign Hero slides 1–2 / Framer / HOT ITEM to fix slide 3 crop
- Expect one far-right subject to survive both full-viewport portrait cover and banner center-cover without a focus field or a recrop
